The '''Afuris''' is the dual-wield version of the {{Weapon|Furis}} automatic pistol, featuring a faster fire rate but less accuracy.

==Characteristics==
*This weapon does primarily {{D|Puncture}} damage.
*Innate {{Pol|Naramon}} polarity.

{{Advantages}}

{{Disadvantages|
*Extremely ammo inefficient; requires exactly 3 reloads to consume all ammo reserves.
}}

{{WeaponComparison|Furis}}
{{WeaponComparison|Dex Furis|header=n}}
{{WeaponComparison|Afuris Prime|header=n}}

==Acquisition==
The Afuris's blueprint can be purchased from the [[Market]].

{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

==Tips==
*Try to limit use according to the situation. Ammunition can be used quickly in a very short amount of time. Ammo pickups are even less effective than with the Furis due to the fixed ammo boost per pickup and the rate of fire.
*Although this weapon is not designed to be used with accuracy, if it is used as a semi-automatic weapon, the bullets always gets close to the center of the sight.
*Using the {{M|Pistol Scavenger}} Aura or {{M|Pistol Ammo Mutation}} mod can help regain lost ammo when needed. Alternatively, bring along [[Squad Ammo Restore]]s.
*Furis mods such as {{M|Winds of Purity}} and [[Riven Mods|Rivens]] cannot be equipped on the Afuris or it's variants.

==Trivia==
*While all the other {{Faction|Tenno}} and [[Prime]] akimbo pistols have prefix Ak-, prefix for akimbo Furis is only A-.

