The '''Akjagara''' are a pair of burst-fire bladed double-barreled pistols, both firing a bullet simultaneously per burst, and primarily focused on delivering {{D|Slash}} damage.

This weapon can be sold for {{cc|5,000}}.

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Slash}} damage.
*Can use the Akjagara-exclusive {{M|Range Advantage}} mod.
*Innate {{Pol|Naramon}} polarity.

{{Advantages|
*Uniquely fires both shots simultaneously instead of consecutively, reducing the chance of one missing.
}}

{{Disadvantages|
*Linearly less efficient &ndash; sometimes a target may only die with three bullets, which requires an entire second burst to be fired.
*Inefficient ammo economy.
}}

{{WeaponComparison|Akjagara Prime}}

==Acquisition==
The Akjagara's blueprint can be purchased from the [[Market]].

{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

==Notes==
*A total of six fully crafted weapons are required to build the Akjagara, those being 2x {{Weapon|Lato}}s, 2x {{Weapon|Bolto}}s, 1x {{Weapon|Akbolto}}, and 1x {{Weapon|Dual Skana}}s. The total process of crafting the weapon will require at least two inventory slots.
*The total crafting cost of the Akjagara, including the blueprint and crafting costs of its prerequisites, is {{cc|210,000}} [[Credits]],  '''7''' {{Resource|Orokin Cell}}s, '''4''' {{Resource|Neurodes}}, '''2''' {{Resource|Morphics}}, '''1,900''' {{Resource|Polymer Bundle}}s, '''850''' {{Resource|Ferrite}}, and '''300''' {{Resource|Alloy Plate}}s, making it one of the weapons with the most numerous crafting materials required to build, and one of the most expensive in terms of Credit cost.
**The total crafting time to build the Akjagara without rushing the construction is: 12 hours to build each {{Weapon|Bolto}} separately for a total of 24 hours, 12 hours to build the {{Weapon|Akbolto}}, and 12 hours to build the Akjagara for a total of 48 hours at minimum, assuming the {{Weapon|Dual Skana}} needed was crafted at any time during the process.

==Tips==
*The Akjagara has a high chance of cutting corpses into pieces, making it a prime candidate for a [[Desecrate|Desecrating]] {{WF|Nekros}} to bring along, as the game considers the cut corpses as separate entities, essentially giving multiple corpses to desecrate from a single enemy and thus yielding more chances to create more drops.
*{{M|Razor Shot}} and {{M|Maim}} are especially effective due to the Akjagara's high ratio of {{D|Slash}} damage.

==Trivia==
*Unlike most dual sidearms, the Akjagara is asymmetrical: the left pistol has its blade on top, while the right pistol has the blade on the bottom.
**These blades are used to reload the weapons; catching the hook end of the blade and extending it forward results in a reload.
*Despite the barrels being in an over/under arrangement, the two shots will usually land side by side of each other.
*The Akjagara is the fourth weapon after the {{Weapon|Redeemer}}, {{Weapon|Tipedo}}, and {{Weapon|Panthera}} to require multiple different weapons as crafting components.
**The Akjagara is also the first dual pistol weapon to require another dual weapon to be crafted, and the first dual weapon where its base crafting weapon components are not two of the single version of the weapon.
*Up until {{Ver|35.1.1}} one of the Akjagara's components, the Akbolto, required a higher Mastery Rank to craft than it (The Akjagara requires Mastery Rank 8, while the Akbolto at the time required Mastery Rank 9).
*The Akjagara is based on the {{Weapon|Tigris}} shotgun's design. The {{Weapon|Redeemer}} gun blade continues this aesthetic with a similar appearance as well.
**All three weapons can be purchased from the [[Razor Gunplay Bundle]].
*Akjagara is the sixth dual secondary to get a [[Akjagara Prime|Primed variant]].
**It is also the fourth burst-fire weapon to get a Primed variant.

==Bugs==
*When performing a quick melee attack to initiate a [[Melee#Finisher|Counterattack Finisher]] while the Akjagara is the active weapon, the Akjagara will appear to be used as the weapon to initiate the attack. However, the actual weapon used will also have its model show up during the attack as well.
*When the weapon levels up, the level up glow effect only shows on the right gun, not the left gun.

